AMDGPU: keep the clamp bit when folding a literal into a carry-out add/sub

Generic (subtargets with integer clamp but no carry-less VALU add/sub:
gfx8; gfx803 is where it was found and tested). Present unchanged in
llvm-project main.

Verified on an RX 590 (gfx803) with llc built from ROCm llvm-project
rocm-6.4.4 (d366fa84) with this patch, compiling the device code that the
shipped clang emits as bitcode: the repro below is right, rocPRIM 3.4.1's
rocprim::merge_sort (struct keys, int32 and int64 values, the default and
four explicit configurations, 1 to 300,000 items) and its block-sort kernel
alone are right and stable, rocPRIM's radix sort is unchanged and right,
and there are no GPU faults. gfx900 and gfx1030 output is byte-identical;
on gfx803 only the instructions at the clamp sites change.
With the full clang-19/libamd_comgr build and PyTorch rebuilt on it:
torch.mode is right at every slice length from 7 to 20,000 in fp16, fp32
and int64, the rocPRIM merge-sort repro has 0 wrong items over 15 cases,
the GEMM shim is bit-identical (46 of 46), PyTorch's OpInfo comparison with
the CPU is unchanged, and the SD 1.5 UNet step and LoRA training run at the
same speed with no GPU faults.

WHY
---
gfx8 has only the carry-out forms of the 32-bit VALU integer add and
subtract (V_ADD_CO_U32, V_SUB_CO_U32, V_SUBREV_CO_U32), so instruction
selection implements a saturating unsigned add or subtract (llvm.uadd.sat,
llvm.usub.sat; InstCombine forms these from `a < b ? 0 : a - b` and the
like) as the VOP3 form of that instruction with the clamp bit set. When the
other operand is a 32-bit literal (not an inline constant), SIFoldOperands
folds it in by shrinking the instruction to its VOP2 form, the only one that
takes a literal on gfx8. VOP2 has no clamp bit and the fold does not check
for one, so the result wraps instead of saturating: usub.sat(x, 1000)
becomes `v_subrev_u32_e32 v, vcc, 0x3e8, v`. SIInstrInfo::canShrink, which
the other shrink paths use, refuses instructions with clamp set; this
special case does not call it. gfx9 and later select the carry-less
V_ADD_U32/V_SUB_U32 for these and keep the clamp.

rocPRIM's device merge sort (rocprim::merge_sort, behind thrust::sort and
sort_by_key for keys that are not plain numbers: c10::Half in torch.sort and
torch.mode, any struct key) is wrong because of this. In the block-level
merge of block_sort_merge, merge_path starts its search at
`diag < input2_size ? 0 : diag - input2_size`. For a full tile, input2_size
is the compile-time half-tile size, 128 or more, so for every thread in the
first half of the tile the start wraps to about 4e9, the search is skipped
and the thread merges from a wrapped LDS index. Every full tile the
block-sort kernel produces is wrong (512 of 1,024 values on the default
configuration), and the merge passes after it inherit that. A partial tile
passes its size at run time, which is why sorts shorter than one tile were
right; the warp-level merge before it uses half sizes of at most 64, inline
constants, and is right.

Repro (hipcc -O2 --offload-arch=gfx803):

  __global__ void k(const unsigned* in, unsigned* out) {
      out[threadIdx.x] = __builtin_elementwise_sub_sat(in[threadIdx.x], 1000u); }

in = 5 gives 4294966301 instead of 0; __builtin_elementwise_add_sat with a
literal overflows to small numbers the same way. Or llc
-mtriple=amdgcn-amd-amdhsa -mcpu=gfx803 on llvm.usub.sat.i32(%x, 1000):
`v_subrev_u32_e32 v2, vcc, 0x3e8, v2`, where gfx900 gives
`s_movk_i32 s2, 0x3e8` and `v_sub_u32_e64 v1, v1, s2 clamp`.

WHAT
----
The carry-op special case in SIFoldOperands::tryAddToFoldList declines the
fold when the instruction has clamp set and restores the operand order, as
its other declining path does. The literal stays in an SGPR and the VOP3
instruction keeps its clamp: one s_movk_i32 or s_mov_b32 per such site.
Instructions without clamp fold as before.

diff -ru a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFoldOperands.cpp b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFoldOperands.cpp
--- a/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFoldOperands.cpp	2026-10-25 20:50:55.625143181 -0700
+++ b/llvm/lib/Target/AMDGPU/SIFoldOperands.cpp	2026-10-25 20:50:55.631621117 -0700
@@ -578,7 +578,11 @@
     if (!TII->isOperandLegal(*MI, CommuteOpNo, OpToFold)) {
       if ((Opc != AMDGPU::V_ADD_CO_U32_e64 && Opc != AMDGPU::V_SUB_CO_U32_e64 &&
            Opc != AMDGPU::V_SUBREV_CO_U32_e64) || // FIXME
-          (!OpToFold->isImm() && !OpToFold->isFI() && !OpToFold->isGlobal())) {
+          (!OpToFold->isImm() && !OpToFold->isFI() && !OpToFold->isGlobal()) ||
+          // The e32 form has no clamp bit, and on subtargets without the
+          // carry-less add/sub a saturating 32-bit add or sub is exactly this
+          // instruction with clamp set: shrinking it would make it wrap.
+          TII->hasModifiersSet(*MI, AMDGPU::OpName::clamp)) {
         TII->commuteInstruction(*MI, false, OpNo, CommuteOpNo);
         return false;
       }
